@startuml KG_AI_Platform_Layer4

title "Layer 4: AI Services / APIs\nComponent Detail  |  Knowledge Graph AI Platform"

' Previous layer: codingAssistance_architecture_L3.puml
' Overview:       codingAssistance_architecture.puml
' Next layer:     codingAssistance_architecture_L5.puml

skinparam backgroundColor   #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontSize   10
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam wrapWidth         260

skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #F8F8F8
  BorderColor     #888888
  FontStyle       bold
  FontSize        11
}

skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor     #555555
  FontSize        10
}

skinparam rectangle<<gateway>> {
  BackgroundColor #F1948A
  BorderColor     #CC0000
  FontStyle       bold
  FontSize        10
}

skinparam rectangle<<external>> {
  BackgroundColor #EFEFEF
  BorderColor     #AAAAAA
  FontSize        9
  FontStyle       italic
}

legend top right
  <b>Legend</b>
  ——→   Synchronous request / active data flow
  - -→   Asynchronous response
endlegend


' ================================================================
' LAYER 4 — AI Services / APIs
' ================================================================
package "Layer 4: AI Services / APIs" as L4 #E8DAEF {

  ' ── API Gateway ─────────────────────────────────────────────
  ' Mandatory enforcement chokepoint.
  ' All traffic from Layer 5 consumers and Layer 6 personas
  ' must pass through this gateway before reaching any service.
  ' Authentication: GitLab / Confluence credentials.
  rectangle "<<API Gateway>>\nAccess Control & Audit\n────────────────────────────────\nAuth: GitLab / Confluence credentials\nAll inbound & outbound traffic enforced here" <<gateway>> as AccessControlGateway

  ' ── Four functional services (behind the gateway) ────────────
  rectangle "Semantic Search API"  as SemanticSearchAPI
  rectangle "Graph Query Service"  as GraphQueryService
  rectangle "RAG Service"          as RAGService
  rectangle "Prompt Orchestrator"  as PromptOrchestrator
}


' ── Inputs from Layer 3 ──────────────────────────────────────────
rectangle "← Layer 3\nNeo4j Knowledge Graph\n(Semantic Search)" <<external>> as In_Neo4j_SS
rectangle "← Layer 3\nNeo4j Knowledge Graph\n(Graph Query)"     <<external>> as In_Neo4j_GQ
rectangle "← Layer 3\nNeo4j Knowledge Graph\n(RAG)"             <<external>> as In_Neo4j_RAG
rectangle "← Layer 3\nNeo4j Knowledge Graph\n(project knowledge / spec areas — Prompt Orchestrator)" <<external>> as In_Neo4j_PO

' ── Inputs from Layer 0 (Prompt Orchestrator — ticket creation) ──
rectangle "← Layer 0\nMarkdown Spec Docs\n(spec areas — ticket creation)" <<external>> as In_L0_Specs

' ── Inputs from Layer 1 (Prompt Orchestrator — ticket creation) ──
rectangle "← Layer 1\nGitLab Monorepo\n(code patterns, Java best practices\n— ticket creation)" <<external>> as In_L1_Code

' ── Inputs from Layer 5 (all consumers via gateway) ──────────────
rectangle "← Layer 5\nAll AI Consumers\n(requests)" <<external>> as In_L5_Consumers

' ── Inputs from Layer 6 (personas — Confluence access) ───────────
rectangle "← Layer 6\nAll Personas\n(read/write/edit Confluence — authenticated)" <<external>> as In_L6_Personas

' ── Outputs to Layer 5 ───────────────────────────────────────────
rectangle "→ Layer 5\nAll AI Consumers\n(responses)" <<external>> as Out_L5_Responses
rectangle "→ Layer 5\nGitLab Issues Board\n(new ticket — To Do column)" <<external>> as Out_GitLabIssues
rectangle "→ Layer 5\nPipeline Service\n(generated prompt — ticket implementation)" <<external>> as Out_PipelineService

' ── Output to Layer 6 ────────────────────────────────────────────
rectangle "→ Layer 6\nadorsys Confluence\n(read/write/edit)" <<external>> as Out_Confluence


' ================================================================
' ARROWS — Inputs from Layer 3 to functional services
' ================================================================

In_Neo4j_SS  --> SemanticSearchAPI
In_Neo4j_GQ  --> GraphQueryService
In_Neo4j_RAG --> RAGService
In_Neo4j_PO  --> PromptOrchestrator : "project knowledge  (coding assistance)\n/ spec areas  (ticket creation)"


' ================================================================
' ARROWS — Cross-layer inputs to Prompt Orchestrator
' ================================================================

In_L0_Specs --> PromptOrchestrator : "spec docs\n(ticket creation)"
In_L1_Code  --> PromptOrchestrator : "existing v1 code patterns\n(read-only, no invention)\n[AccountController=v1, AccountControllerV2=v2]"
In_L1_Code  --> PromptOrchestrator : "latest Java version &\nbest practices"


' ================================================================
' ARROWS — Layer 5 consumers → Gateway → functional services
' ================================================================

In_L5_Consumers --> AccessControlGateway

AccessControlGateway --> SemanticSearchAPI
AccessControlGateway --> GraphQueryService
AccessControlGateway --> RAGService
AccessControlGateway --> PromptOrchestrator


' ================================================================
' ARROWS — Layer 6 personas → Gateway → Prompt Orchestrator
' ================================================================

In_L6_Personas --> AccessControlGateway : "read/write/edit Confluence request"
' AccessControlGateway → PromptOrchestrator already drawn above.


' ================================================================
' ARROWS — Response path  (service → gateway → Layer 5 consumer)
' Responses are asynchronous — shown as dashed arrows.
' ================================================================

SemanticSearchAPI  ..> AccessControlGateway : "[response]"
GraphQueryService  ..> AccessControlGateway : "[response]"
RAGService         ..> AccessControlGateway : "[response]"
PromptOrchestrator ..> AccessControlGateway : "[response]"

AccessControlGateway ..> Out_L5_Responses


' ================================================================
' ARROWS — Prompt Orchestrator outputs
' ================================================================

' Ticket creation (Case 3): Prompt Orchestrator creates a new ticket
' on the To Do column of the GitLab Issues Board.
PromptOrchestrator --> Out_GitLabIssues : "new ticket  (To Do column)\n(ticket creation)"

' Ticket implementation (Case 2): Prompt Orchestrator returns a
' generated prompt to the Pipeline Service.
PromptOrchestrator ..> Out_PipelineService : "generated prompt\n(ticket implementation)"

' Confluence access (Fix D): Prompt Orchestrator reads or writes
' Confluence pages on behalf of the requesting persona.
PromptOrchestrator --> Out_Confluence : "read / write / edit"


' ================================================================
' NOTE — Architecture decision required
' ================================================================
note as NoteAudit #FFE0E0
  <b>Architecture Decision Required: Audit Log Destination</b>
  The API Gateway captures access and audit events.
  The destination for these audit logs has not yet been
  specified  (e.g. SIEM, centralised log store, Loki).
  No arrow is drawn until this is confirmed.
end note


' ================================================================
' NOTE — Prompt Orchestrator call patterns
' ================================================================
note as NotePromptOrch
  <b>Prompt Orchestrator — three call patterns</b>

  Case 1  (human-initiated, coding assistance)
    Developer → IDE Extensions → Gateway → Prompt Orchestrator
    Prompt Orchestrator uses project knowledge from Neo4j
    to construct a prompt → returns result to IDE Extensions.

  Case 2  (pipeline-initiated, ticket implementation)
    GitLab Issues Board → Pipeline Service → Gateway
    → Prompt Orchestrator  (input: ticket description)
    Prompt Orchestrator generates a prompt to implement the
    ticket → returns generated prompt to Pipeline Service.

  Case 3  (pipeline-initiated, ticket creation)
    Pipeline Service → Gateway → Prompt Orchestrator
    Inputs: spec docs (L0 + L3), existing code patterns (L1),
            Java best practices (L1)
    Prompt Orchestrator creates a new ticket on the
    GitLab Issues Board  (To Do column).
end note

@enduml
